\ crypto/bip39_test.fam — BIP39 (crypto/bip39.fam, crypto/sha256.fam)
\ against Python (the standard, from the same word list: values written
\ by this file's generator in the commit that added it): SHA-256 of 0, 3
\ and 16 bytes; five entropies (the standard's first, 7f..., 80..., ff...
\ and one more): the phrase, the entropy back from it, the seed with
\ "TREZOR", one with none; a phrase in mixed case and spacing taken, its
\ seed the same; 11 words, a word not in the list, a wrong checksum
\ refused.  Prints "bip39: N as expected, M not".

: tpas variable ;  : tfai variable ;  : tex variable ;  : tout variable ;  : tent variable ;  : txp variable ;
: tchk  swap if drop tpas @ 1 lit + tpas ! else "bip39: " puts puts 0A lit putc tfai @ 1 lit + tfai ! then ;   \ ( flag str -- )
: tx  tex @ txp @ + c!  txp @ 1 lit + txp ! ;
: tsame  ( a b n -- flag )  -1 lit swap 0 lit do 2 lit pick i + c@ 2 lit pick i + c@ = and loop nip nip ;
80 lit alloc tex !  200 lit alloc tout !  20 lit alloc tent !
